[
  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186124469,
      "id": "0096e314-e53e-5d9b-9cee-fe34fa3a6379",
      "title": "Applying the Vector Form of the Chain Rule to a Function of Two Variables"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "29158531-7e0f-5d95-acf0-124e827bb83b",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x{y}^{2})$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)={e}^{4t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\,\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x{y}^{2}))\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(x{y}^{2}))\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 0)}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{(0{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 1)}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2xy}{1+{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{4t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{2}}{1+({e}^{4t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2({e}^{4t})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)}{1+({e}^{4t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sin^{2}⁡3t}{1+{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}{1+{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{4t})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =4{e}^{4t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{\\sin^{2}⁡3t}{1+{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{2{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t}{1+{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}\\,\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (4{e}^{4t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+3\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\,\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{4t}\\sin^{2}⁡3t}{1+{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}+\\frac{6{e}^{4t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t}{1+{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{4t}(4\\sin^{2}⁡3t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t)}{1+{e}^{8t}\\sin^{4}⁡3t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "004b671b-9186-5d58-8522-188866dbc506",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "797cf2a7-6321-5111-95e3-58c2ac3050fe",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{2 \\left(2 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) e^{4 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}}{e^{8 t} \\sin^{4}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "1aaa7d7d-e28e-5ac4-8f11-5a1e13dfc117",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "\\frac{4 e^{4 t} \\sin^{2}{\\left(3 t \\right)}}{e^{8 t} \\sin^{4}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 1}"
            },
            {
              ":answer/id": "7e810c3d-faf6-5d8d-b8fd-30ff17bdf646",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "- \\frac{2 \\left(- 2 \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 3 \\cos{\\left(3 t \\right)}\\right) e^{4 t} \\sin{\\left(3 t \\right)}}{e^{8 t} \\sin^{4}{\\left(3 t \\right)} + 1}"
            },
            {
