    "question": {
      ":question/id": "952141cb-fc2a-50c0-a8ac-a7a34d104b08",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "If $f(x,y)=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x{y}^{2})$ and $\\mathbf{r}(t)={e}^{2t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t\\,\\mathbf{j},$ compute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))].$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The chain rule in vector form states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))]=∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t).\n$$\n\nFirst, we need to compute $∇f(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x{y}^{2}))\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(4x{y}^{2}))\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(1{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 0)}{1+16{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{4(0{y}^{2}+x2y\\cdot 1)}{1+16{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{1+16{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{8xy}{1+16{x}^{2}{y}^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute $x={e}^{2t}$ and $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t$ into the above to find $∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t)) & =\\frac{4(\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)^{2}}{1+16({e}^{2t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{8({e}^{2t})(\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)}{1+16({e}^{2t})^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)^{4}}\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\sin^{2}⁡5t}{1+16{e}^{4t}\\sin^{4}⁡5t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{8{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t}{1+16{e}^{4t}\\sin^{4}⁡5t}\\,\\mathbf{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the derivative of $\\mathbf{r}(t),$ which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{2t})\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)\\,\\mathbf{j} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\,\\mathbf{j}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, applying the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}[f(\\mathbf{r}(t))] & =∇f(\\mathbf{r}(t))\\cdot {\\mathbf{r}}^{′}(t) \\\\  & =(\\frac{4\\sin^{2}⁡5t}{1+16{e}^{4t}\\sin^{4}⁡5t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+\\frac{8{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t}{1+16{e}^{4t}\\sin^{4}⁡5t}\\,\\mathbf{j})\\cdot (2{e}^{2t}\\,\\mathbf{i}+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\,\\mathbf{j}) \\\\  & =\\frac{8{e}^{2t}\\sin^{2}⁡5t}{1+16{e}^{4t}\\sin^{4}⁡5t}+\\frac{40{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t}{1+16{e}^{4t}\\sin^{4}⁡5t} \\\\  & =\\frac{4{e}^{2t}(2\\sin^{2}⁡5t+10\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t)}{1+16{e}^{4t}\\sin^{4}⁡5t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "d7423c9b-910b-549f-834c-d396cf528d24",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
